.el .ds Aq '
.TH geectl-prjconf-clean 1  "geectl-prjconf-clean 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-prjconf\-clean \- Clean a project\*(Aqs prjconf. A mutation: dry\-run is the default. Shares validate\*(Aqs credential gate and 32\-repository bound
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl prjconf clean\fR [\fB\-\-include\-path\-dependent\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPROJECT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clean a project\*(Aqs prjconf. A mutation: dry\-run is the default. Shares validate\*(Aqs credential gate and 32\-repository bound.
.PP
A prjconf is inherited: downstream projects concatenate this config with different repository paths, architectures and `_repository` / `_project` values. By default clean removes only lines proven dead independent of the repository path and architecture (same\-line duplicate tokens and unconditionally overridden `Substitute` lines); `\-\-include\-path\-dependent` also removes lines proven dead in every repository and architecture evaluation of this project.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-path\-dependent\fR
Also remove lines proven dead only in this project\*(Aqs own repository and architecture evaluations
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIPROJECT\fR>
The project to clean the prjconf of
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
